The  command  drops the TCP connection specified by the local ad‐
dress port and the foreign address port Addresses and  ports  can
be  specified  by  name  or numeric value.  If a connection to is
causing congestion on a network link, one can drop the  TCP  ses‐
sion   in  charge:  $  fstat  |  grep  ’httpd.*internet.*‐‐’  www
httpd      21307    3* internet stream tcp  \          0xd1007ca8
192.168.5.41:80  ‐‐  192.168.5.1:26747 The following command will
drop the connection: # tcpdrop 192.168.5.41 80 192.168.5.1 26747
